Theorem CN-6: Wide-locality uniqueness ceiling

  Preconditions:
    - s is an AimsState per the canonical proof notation
      sec-Per-Dimension-Symbol-Set
    - s.locality is at least HeapEscaping (HeapEscaping or Unknown)
    - s.uniqueness = u (Unique)
    - canonicalize(s) is s with CN-6 applied per Annex E §AIMS + sec-1.8 L-6 monotonicity
    - Exception clause for return values not in scope of this shape;
      see the canonical proof notation sec-Return-Provenance

  Soundness property:
    Forall s in AimsState.
      (s.locality >= HeapEscaping and s.uniqueness = u)
      implies
      canonicalize(s).uniqueness = ms

  Proof obligation:
    Case analysis on s.locality (active locality >= HeapEscaping):
      Case s.locality = HeapEscaping:
        CN-6 fires: Uniqueness := ms (MaybeShared);
        result canonical; other dimensions preserved per Annex E §AIMS (CN-6 mutates only Uniqueness).
      Case s.locality = Unknown:
        CN-6 fires (uses >= per the rule's >= ordering covering Unknown);
        Uniqueness := ms; result canonical.

    Lattice validation:
      Uniqueness dimension carrier: u < ms < s (height 2);
      CN-6 moves Uniqueness UP the dimension (u -> ms);
      monotone per L-6 on the demotion step.

    Idempotence (L-7):
      After CN-6 fires, s.uniqueness = ms; CN-6 premise no longer
      holds (uniqueness != u); second canonicalize round is no-op;
      idempotent in 1 round.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (for the HeapEscaping / Unknown enumeration above)
      lattice (validates state-canonical post-CN-6 + L-7 idempotence)

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: CN-shape scaffold-time; engine implementation pending
